7. SaaS entitlement follows the merchant's approved policy.

## 8. Upgrade, downgrade, and plan changes

Plan changes are important to SaaS revenue expansion and retention.

### Example commercial scenario

A customer moves from Growth to Business.

| Item | Growth | Business |
|---|---:|---:|
| Monthly fee | Rp299,000 | Rp799,000 |
| Change | — | Upgrade |
| Difference | — | Rp500,000 |

### Decisions required

- Does the new price take effect immediately or next cycle?
- Is the price difference prorated?
- Is an immediate additional charge required?
- Does the customer need to authorize another payment?
- Are existing billing obligations affected?
- Does the new plan activate immediately?
- How are downgrades handled?
- What happens to unused services or allowances?

### Capability status

| Requirement | Status |
|---|---|
| Separate Plans and Pricing | Configuration capability; validate exact behavior |
| Commercial plan-change policy | Merchant-defined |
| Native plan-change API | Validate; do not assume availability |
| Automatic proration | Validate; do not assume availability |
| Entitlement update | Merchant-side integration unless confirmed otherwise |
| Historical billing preservation | Define and test |

A merchant can implement plan changes in its own application while coordinating the resulting billing configuration and payment obligations with FlexiBill.

## 9. Failed payment and churn prevention

### Typical failure scenarios

| Scenario | Recommended action |
|---|---|
| Insufficient funds | Notify customer and follow permitted recovery policy |
| Expired payment credential | Request payment-method update |
| Bank or issuer decline | Explain the next action |
| Authorization issue | Guide customer through an eligible authorization flow |
| Technical failure | Investigate before retry |
| Customer intentionally cancels | Apply cancellation policy |
| Subscription and payment status mismatch | Reconcile before entitlement changes |

### Recovery journey

```text id="b6x2mt"
       RECURRING BILLING
              |
              v
       PAYMENT FAILURE
              |
              v
       FAILURE CLASSIFIED
              |
              v
      CUSTOMER NOTIFICATION
              |
              v
       RECOVERY OPPORTUNITY
              |
        +-----+-----+
        |           |
        v           v
    PAYMENT      NO PAYMENT
    SUCCESS        |
        |          v
        v      MERCHANT POLICY
    RESTORE /       |
    MAINTAIN        v
    ENTITLEMENT  RESTRICT / CANCEL
                 AS APPROVED
```

The SaaS merchant owns the decision to maintain, restrict, or terminate service access. FlexiBill payment status alone should not be treated as the complete entitlement decision.

