## 11. Usage-based and hybrid SaaS billing

Some SaaS merchants combine a recurring base fee with usage charges.

Illustrative example:

| Component | Example |
|---|---:|
| Monthly platform fee | Rp299,000 |
| Included API calls | 10,000 |
| Additional API calls | Merchant-defined |
| Storage overage | Merchant-defined |
| Premium support | Rp100,000 |

The SaaS platform should measure and calculate actual usage unless a separate metering and aggregation capability has been implemented and validated.

### Capability distinction

| Capability | Internal position |
|---|---|
| Flat recurring subscription | Supported configuration model subject to validation |
| Per-unit pricing | Pricing model available; validate calculation requirements |
| Tiered / volume / stairstep pricing | Pricing models available; validate exact commercial calculation |
| Native real-time metering | Gap / future direction |
| Usage aggregation | Merchant-side or integration requirement |
| Automated usage-to-invoice workflow | Requires end-to-end validation |
| Entitlement management | Merchant-side responsibility unless separately integrated |

Do not describe FlexiBill as a complete usage-based billing platform without confirming metering, aggregation, and calculation responsibilities.

